[2026-03-14T21:07:26.831Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MMYTCZa1GoWucbG3c9noke","type":"tool_result","content":"   113→## Navigation Sidebar\n   114→\n   115→**Components**: Sidebar, SidebarCollapse, KeyboardShortcuts\n   116→\n   117→### Sidebar\n   118→\n   119→#### Test: Sidebar renders workspace header\n   120→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n   121→- **Expected**: The sidebar displays the workspace name at the top. The workspace name is clickable.\n   122→\n   123→#### Test: Sidebar workspace header navigates to home\n   124→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and viewing `/team/1/issues`\n   125→- **Action**: User clicks the workspace name in the sidebar header\n   126→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/my-issues` (home page).\n   127→\n   128→#### Test: Sidebar renders main navigation links\n   129→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n   130→- **Expected**: The sidebar shows \"My Issues\" with a user-circle icon and \"Inbox\" with an inbox icon. Both are clickable navigation links.\n   131→\n   132→#### Test: Sidebar My Issues link navigates correctly\n   133→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/inbox`\n   134→- **Action**: User clicks \"My Issues\" in the sidebar\n   135→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/my-issues`. The \"My Issues\" link appears selected/active with visual distinction (e.g., highlighted background).\n   136→\n   137→#### Test: Sidebar Inbox link navigates correctly\n   138→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n   139→- **Action**: User clicks \"Inbox\" in the sidebar\n   140→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/inbox`. The \"Inbox\" link appears selected/active.\n   141→\n   142→#### Test: Sidebar Inbox shows unread notification count badge\n   143→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 unread notifications\n   144→- **Expected**: The \"Inbox\" link in the sidebar displays a badge showing \"3\". The badge is visually distinct (e.g., accent color background).\n   145→\n   146→#### Test: Sidebar Inbox badge updates when notifications are read\n   147→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 3 unread notifications, badge shows \"3\"\n   148→- **Action**: User navigates to `/inbox` and marks one notification as read\n   149→- **Expected**: The badge count updates to \"2\". If all notifications are read, the badge disappears.\n   150→\n   151→#### Test: Sidebar Inbox badge not shown when no unread notifications\n   152→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has 0 unread notifications\n   153→- **Expected**: No badge is shown next to the \"Inbox\" link.\n   154→\n   155→#### Test: Sidebar renders team sections\n   156→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, workspace has teams \"Engineering\" and \"Design\"\n   157→- **Expected**: The sidebar displays a \"Team Section\" with each team name as a collapsible section header. Under each team: \"Issues\" (list icon), \"Active Cycle\" (refresh-cw icon), \"Projects\" (folder icon), \"Views\" (layout icon).\n   158→\n   159→#### Test: Sidebar team section is collapsible\n   160→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team section is expanded\n   161→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Engineering\" team section header\n   162→- **Expected**: The team section collapses, hiding Issues, Active Cycle, Projects, and Views sub-links. Clicking again expands it back.\n   163→\n   164→#### Test: Sidebar team section collapse toggles multiple times\n   165→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team section is expanded\n   166→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Engineering\" header to collapse, then clicks it again to expand, then collapses it once more\n   167→- **Expected**: Each click toggles the section correctly. After three clicks the section is collapsed.\n   168→\n   169→#### Test: Sidebar team Issues link navigates to team issues page\n   170→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n   171→- **Action**: User clicks \"Issues\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n   172→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/team/eng-1/issues`. The link appears selected/active.\n   173→\n   174→#### Test: Sidebar team Active Cycle link navigates to cycles page\n   175→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n   176→- **Action**: User clicks \"Active Cycle\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n   177→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/team/eng-1/cycles`.\n   178→\n   179→#### Test: Sidebar team Projects link navigates to team projects\n   180→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n   181→- **Action**: User clicks \"Projects\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n   182→- **Expected**: User is navigated to the projects page filtered by this team, or to `/projects` with the team filter applied.\n   183→\n   184→#### Test: Sidebar team Views link navigates to saved views\n   185→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Engineering\" team has id \"eng-1\"\n   186→- **Action**: User clicks \"Views\" under the \"Engineering\" team section\n   187→- **Expected**: User is navigated to a views page for the team showing saved filtered views.\n   188→\n   189→#### Test: Sidebar renders workspace section links\n   190→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated\n   191→- **Expected**: The sidebar displays a \"Workspace\" section with links: \"All Projects\" (folder icon), \"All Teams\" (users icon), \"Members\" (user-plus icon), \"Labels\" (tag icon), \"Settings\" (settings icon).\n   192→\n   193→#### Test: Sidebar All Projects link navigates correctly\n   194→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   195→- **Action**: User clicks \"All Projects\" in the workspace section\n   196→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/projects`.\n   197→\n   198→#### Test: Sidebar All Teams link navigates correctly\n   199→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   200→- **Action**: User clicks \"All Teams\" in the workspace section\n   201→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/teams`.\n   202→\n   203→#### Test: Sidebar Members link navigates correctly\n   204→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   205→- **Action**: User clicks \"Members\" in the workspace section\n   206→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/members`.\n   207→\n   208→#### Test: Sidebar Labels link navigates correctly\n   209→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   210→- **Action**: User clicks \"Labels\" in the workspace section\n   211→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings/labels`.\n   212→\n   213→#### Test: Sidebar Settings link navigates correctly\n   214→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`\n   215→- **Action**: User clicks \"Settings\" in the workspace section\n   216→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/settings`.\n   217→\n   218→#### Test: Sidebar highlights current page link\n   219→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`\n   220→- **Expected**: The \"My Issues\" link in the sidebar has an active/selected visual style (e.g., highlighted background, different text color). Other links do not have the active style.\n   221→\n   222→#### Test: Sidebar active highlight updates on navigation\n   223→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, on `/my-issues`, \"My Issues\" is highlighted\n   224→- **Action**: User clicks \"Inbox\" in the sidebar\n   225→- **Expected**: \"Inbox\" becomes highlighted and \"My Issues\" loses its highlight.\n   226→\n   227→#### Test: Sidebar is present on all authenticated pages\n   228→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated\n   229→- **Action**: User navigates to `/my-issues`, then `/inbox`, then `/settings`\n   230→- **Expected**: The sidebar is visible and functional on all three pages with consistent layout and content.\n   231→\n   232→#### Test: Sidebar is not shown on login page\n   233→- **Initial state**: User is not authenticated\n   234→- **Action**: User navigates to `/login`\n   235→- **Expected**: The sidebar is not visible. Only the login form is shown.\n   236→\n   237→#### Test: Sidebar is not shown on signup page\n   238→- **Initial state**: User is not authenticated\n   239→- **Action**: User navigates to `/signup`\n   240→- **Expected**: The sidebar is not visible. Only the signup form is shown.\n   241→\n   242→### SidebarCollapse\n   243→\n   244→#### Test: Sidebar collapse toggle button is visible\n   245→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is expanded\n   246→- **Expected**: A toggle button is visible on the sidebar (e.g., a chevron-left icon or hamburger icon) that can collapse the sidebar.\n   247→\n   248→#### Test: Sidebar collapses to icon-only mode\n   249→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is fully expanded showing labels and icons\n   250→- **Action**: User clicks the sidebar collapse toggle button\n   251→- **Expected**: The sidebar collapses to icon-only mode. Navigation items show only their icons without text labels. The sidebar width is significantly reduced. The main content area expands to fill the freed space.\n   252→\n   253→#### Test: Sidebar expands from icon-only mode\n   254→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is in icon-only (collapsed) mode\n   255→- **Action**: User clicks the sidebar expand toggle button\n   256→- **Expected**: The sidebar expands back to full width showing both icons and text labels. The main content area shrinks accordingly.\n   257→\n   258→#### Test: Sidebar collapse state persists across navigation\n   259→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is collapsed to icon-only mode\n   260→- **Action**: User clicks the \"My Issues\" icon in the collapsed sidebar, then clicks the \"Inbox\" icon\n   261→- **Expected**: The sidebar remains in collapsed icon-only mode through both navigations. It does not re-expand on page change.\n   262→\n   263→#### Test: Sidebar icons are still clickable in collapsed mode\n   264→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is in icon-only mode, user is on `/my-issues`\n   265→- **Action**: User clicks the Inbox icon in the collapsed sidebar\n   266→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/inbox`. The navigation works identically to the expanded sidebar.\n   267→\n   268→#### Test: Sidebar collapse toggle works multiple times in sequence\n   269→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is expanded\n   270→- **Action**: User clicks the collapse toggle, then clicks it again, then clicks it once more\n   271→- **Expected**: Sidebar collapses, then expands, then collapses again. Each transition is smooth (animated, ~150ms). The toggle works reliably on repeated use.\n   272→\n   273→#### Test: Sidebar team sections visible in collapsed mode\n   274→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is in icon-only mode, workspace has team \"Engineering\"\n   275→- **Expected**: Team navigation items are still accessible in icon-only mode (icons for Issues, Active Cycle, Projects, Views are visible and clickable).\n   276→\n   277→#### Test: Sidebar workspace section visible in collapsed mode\n   278→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, sidebar is in icon-only mode\n   279→- **Expected**: Workspace section items (All Projects, All Teams, Members, Labels, Settings) are visible as icons and remain clickable.\n   280→\n   281→### KeyboardShortcuts\n   282→\n   283→#### Test: Pressing C opens create issue modal\n   284→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, no modal is open, focus is not in a text input\n   285→- **Action**: User presses the \"C\" key\n   286→- **Expected**: The create issue modal opens with the title field focused.\n   287→\n   288→#### Test: Pressing C does not open modal when typing in input\n   289→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, focus is in a text input field (e.g., a search field or comment box)\n   290→- **Action**: User presses the \"C\" key\n   291→- **Expected**: The character \"c\" is typed into the input field. The create issue modal does NOT open.\n   292→\n   293→#### Test: G then I navigates to My Issues\n   294→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/inbox`, focus is not in a text input\n   295→- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then presses \"I\" key\n   296→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/my-issues`.\n   297→\n   298→#### Test: G then N navigates to Inbox\n   299→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, focus is not in a text input\n   300→- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then presses \"N\" key\n   301→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/inbox`.\n   302→\n   303→#### Test: G then I does not navigate when typing in input\n   304→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, focus is in a text input field\n   305→- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then \"I\" key\n   306→- **Expected**: The characters \"gi\" are typed into the input. No navigation occurs.\n   307→\n   308→#### Test: G chord times out if second key is delayed\n   309→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, focus is not in a text input\n   310→- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, waits 2 seconds, then presses \"I\" key\n   311→- **Expected**: No navigation occurs. The chord is cancelled after a short timeout (~1 second).\n   312→\n   313→#### Test: G followed by unrecognized key does nothing\n   314→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/my-issues`, focus is not in a text input\n   315→- **Action**: User presses \"G\" key, then presses \"X\" key\n   316→- **Expected**: Nothing happens. No navigation or modal opens. The app does not error.\n   317→\n   318→#### Test: Keyboard shortcuts work from different pages\n   319→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated and on `/settings`\n   320→- **Action**: User presses \"C\" key\n   321→- **Expected**: The create issue modal opens, same as from any other page.\n   322→\n   323→#### Test: Keyboard shortcuts do not fire when modal is open\n   324→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, create issue modal is open\n   325→- **Action**: User presses \"G\" then \"I\"\n   326→- **Expected**: No navigation occurs. The modal remains open. The keystrokes do not trigger navigation shortcuts.\n   327→\n   328→## My Issues Page (`/my-issues`)\n   329→\n   330→**Components**: MyIssuesList, IssueRow, FiltersToolbar\n   331→\n   332→### MyIssuesList\n   333→\n   334→#### Test: My Issues page renders with issues grouped by status\n   335→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues assigned in statuses: Backlog (2 issues), In Progress (1 issue), Done (1 issue)\n   336→- **Expected**: The page displays issues grouped under status headers. Each group header shows the status icon, status name, and issue count in parentheses. Groups appear in status order: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled. Empty status groups are not displayed.\n   337→\n   338→#### Test: My Issues page shows empty state when no issues assigned\n   339→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has no issues assigned to them\n   340→- **Expected**: The page displays a friendly empty state message with an icon (e.g., \"No issues assigned to you yet\") instead of an empty list.\n   341→\n   342→#### Test: Status group is collapsible\n   343→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in \"In Progress\" status, the group is expanded\n   344→- **Action**: User clicks the \"In Progress\" group header\n   345→- **Expected**: The group collapses, hiding all issues within it. The group header remains visible with a collapse indicator (e.g., chevron rotates). Clicking again expands the group back.\n   346→\n   347→#### Test: Status group collapse toggles multiple times\n   348→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Backlog\" group is expanded with 2 issues\n   349→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Backlog\" header to collapse, clicks it again to expand, then collapses once more\n   350→- **Expected**: Each click toggles correctly. After three clicks, the group is collapsed and its issues are hidden. The count in parentheses remains accurate.\n   351→\n   352→#### Test: Multiple status groups can be independently collapsed\n   353→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, has issues in Backlog, In Progress, and Done groups, all expanded\n   354→- **Action**: User collapses the \"Backlog\" group, then collapses the \"Done\" group\n   355→- **Expected**: \"Backlog\" and \"Done\" groups are collapsed while \"In Progress\" remains expanded showing its issues.\n   356→\n   357→#### Test: My Issues page only shows issues assigned to current user\n   358→- **Initial state**: User \"Alice\" is authenticated. Issue ENG-1 is assigned to Alice, Issue ENG-2 is assigned to \"Bob\", Issue ENG-3 is unassigned.\n   359→- **Expected**: Only ENG-1 appears on Alice's My Issues page. ENG-2 and ENG-3 do not appear.\n   360→\n   361→#### Test: My Issues page updates when issue is assigned to user\n   362→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/my-issues` with 2 issues\n   363→- **Action**: Another user assigns a new issue to the current user (or user creates an issue assigned to themselves via the create modal)\n   364→- **Expected**: The new issue appears in the appropriate status group on the My Issues page without requiring a manual refresh.\n   365→\n   366→#### Test: My Issues page title and header are displayed\n   367→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, navigates to `/my-issues`\n   368→- **Expected**: The page shows a header/title \"My Issues\" at the top of the main content area, clearly identifying the current page.\n   369→\n   370→### IssueRow\n   371→\n   372→#### Test: Issue row displays all required fields\n   373→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing My Issues. Issue ENG-42 exists with title \"Fix login bug\", status \"In Progress\", priority \"High\", labels [\"Bug\"], assignee avatar, due date \"2026-03-20\", project \"Auth Rewrite\".\n   374→- **Expected**: The issue row displays: High priority icon (orange arrow-up), identifier \"ENG-42\", title \"Fix login bug\", In Progress status icon (yellow half circle), \"Bug\" label as a small colored badge, assignee avatar, due date \"Mar 20\", and project name \"Auth Rewrite\".\n   375→\n   376→#### Test: Issue row title is clickable and navigates to issue detail\n   377→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing My Issues with issue ENG-42\n   378→- **Action**: User clicks on the title \"Fix login bug\" in the issue row\n   379→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/issue/<issueId>` for issue ENG-42. The issue detail page loads.\n   380→\n   381→#### Test: Issue row status icon is clickable to change status\n   382→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing My Issues. Issue ENG-42 has status \"Todo\" (circle icon, gray).\n   383→- **Action**: User clicks the status icon on the ENG-42 issue row\n   384→- **Expected**: A dropdown/popover appears showing all available statuses (Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled) with their respective icons and colors.\n   385→\n   386→#### Test: Changing status via issue row status dropdown persists\n   387→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing My Issues. Issue ENG-42 has status \"Todo\". User has clicked the status icon and the dropdown is open.\n   388→- **Action**: User selects \"In Progress\" from the status dropdown\n   389→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. The issue row now shows the In Progress icon (yellow half circle). The issue moves from the \"Todo\" group to the \"In Progress\" group. The change is persisted to the database.\n   390→\n   391→#### Test: Issue row status change updates group membership\n   392→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, \"Todo\" group has 3 issues including ENG-42, \"In Progress\" group has 1 issue\n   393→- **Action**: User changes ENG-42's status from \"Todo\" to \"In Progress\" via the status icon dropdown\n   394→- **Expected**: ENG-42 moves from the \"Todo\" group to the \"In Progress\" group. \"Todo\" group now shows count of 2, \"In Progress\" shows count of 2.\n   395→\n   396→#### Test: Issue row status dropdown can be used multiple times\n   397→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 has status \"Todo\"\n   398→- **Action**: User clicks status icon, changes to \"In Progress\", then clicks status icon again, changes to \"Done\"\n   399→- **Expected**: Both status changes work correctly. The issue ends up in the \"Done\" group with a green check circle icon. Each dropdown opens and closes cleanly.\n   400→\n   401→#### Test: Issue row displays priority icon with correct color\n   402→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing My Issues with issues at different priorities\n   403→- **Expected**: Urgent shows red alert-triangle icon, High shows orange arrow-up, Medium shows yellow minus, Low shows blue arrow-down, No Priority shows gray dots-horizontal.\n   404→\n   405→#### Test: Issue row displays labels as colored badges\n   406→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 has labels \"Bug\" (red) and \"Frontend\" (blue)\n   407→- **Expected**: Both labels are shown as small colored badges in the issue row, each with the label's color and name text.\n   408→\n   409→#### Test: Issue row shows assignee avatar\n   410→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issue ENG-42 is assigned to \"Jane Doe\" who has an avatar\n   411→- **Expected**: The issue row shows Jane Doe's avatar as a small circular image. If no avatar, shows initials.\n   412→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014eR7wVX7AcLMUqBVwwRoLL","session_id":"082cad4c-aeb8-4793-9f14-2c9a8624c360","uuid":"ace22e16-12b5-4bcf-ad30-d518d33151a3"}
