[2026-03-14T21:08:20.046Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KKkME1JvERX5U4kAf57VDJ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information you need. Here's a comprehensive summary of the files found:\n\n## Summary of LinearClone API Endpoints and Components\n\n### 1. Notifications API Endpoint\n**File:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/notifications.ts`\n\nThis endpoint handles:\n- **GET /api/notifications** - Get all non-archived notifications for the authenticated user\n  - Returns list of notifications with fields: id, type, issue_id, description, read, archived, created_at, issue_identifier, issue_title\n  - Requires Bearer token authentication\n  \n- **PUT /api/notifications/{notificationId}/read** - Mark a single notification as read\n  - Updates the `read` field to true\n  - Returns `{ success: true }`\n  \n- **PUT /api/notifications/{notificationId}/archive** - Archive a notification\n  - Updates the `archived` field to true\n  - Returns `{ success: true }`\n\n### 2. Notifications Count API Endpoint\n**File:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/notifications-count.ts`\n\n- **GET /api/notifications-count** - Get count of unread, non-archived notifications\n  - Returns `{ count: number }`\n  - Requires Bearer token authentication\n\n### 3. Auth/Login API Endpoint\n**File:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/login.ts`\n\n- **POST /api/login** - Authenticate user and get session token\n  - Request body: `{ email: string, password: string }`\n  - Response: `{ user: { id, name, email }, token: string }`\n  - Token is valid for 30 days\n  - Uses PBKDF2 password hashing with SHA-512\n\n### 4. Teams API Endpoint\n**File:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/teams.ts`\n\n- **GET /api/teams** - List all teams with metadata\n  - Returns: `{ teams: Array<{ id, name, identifier, description, member_count, active_cycle_name }> }`\n  - Use this to get dynamic team IDs\n  \n- **GET /api/teams/{teamId}** - Get specific team details with members\n  - Returns: `{ team, members, availableMembers }`\n  \n- **POST /api/teams** - Create new team\n- **PUT /api/teams/{teamId}** - Update team\n- **DELETE /api/teams/{teamId}** - Delete team\n\n### 5. Inbox Page Component\n**File:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/Inbox.tsx`\n\nThe Inbox page:\n- Displays notifications via `<NotificationList>` component\n- Uses Redux state for notifications, loading state, and unreadCount\n- Fetches notifications on mount if token exists\n- Shows unread count badge in the title\n\n### 6. Notification Display & Marking As Read\n\n**NotificationList Component** (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/NotificationList.tsx`):\n- Displays list of notification rows\n- Shows \"You're all caught up!\" when no notifications\n- Displays unread count in header\n\n**NotificationRow Component** (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/NotificationRow.tsx`):\n- Renders individual notification with type icon, issue identifier, description, timestamp\n- On click: marks notification as read (if not already) and navigates to issue detail\n- Archive button: removes notification from list\n- Supports keyboard navigation (Enter key)\n\n**Redux Slice** (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/notificationsSlice.ts`):\n- `fetchNotifications()` - Gets all notifications via `/api/notifications`\n- `markNotificationRead(notificationId)` - Marks as read via `/api/notifications/{id}/read`\n- `archiveNotification(notificationId)` - Archives via `/api/notifications/{id}/archive`\n- `fetchUnreadCount()` - Gets count via `/api/notifications-count`\n- Manages state: items[], unreadCount, loading\n\n### 7. Playwright Configuration\n**File:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n\nKey configuration:\n- Test directory: `./tests`\n- Base URL: `http://localhost:8888`\n- Timeout: 60 seconds (actions 15 seconds)\n- Uses Replay.io for recording\n- Reporter: Replay, JSON, and HTML\n- Uses Chromium with Replay devices\n- Fully parallel execution"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a9bbab1cdb6ec8ea7 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 35883\ntool_uses: 13\nduration_ms: 16013</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"082cad4c-aeb8-4793-9f14-2c9a8624c360","uuid":"852ebcb9-1270-423f-a4b2-e165343f3b7a","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /repo/apps/LinearClone/, I need to find:\n1. The notifications API endpoint (netlify/functions/) - how to get notifications, mark as read, get unread count\n2. The auth/login API endpoint - how to get a session token\n3. The teams API endpoint - how to list teams (to get dynamic team IDs)\n4. The Inbox page component - how notifications are displayed and marked as read\n5. The playwright.config.ts file\n\nRead the full content of each file found.","agentId":"a9bbab1cdb6ec8ea7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information you need. Here's a comprehensive summary of the files found:\n\n## Summary of LinearClone API Endpoints and Components\n\n### 1. Notifications API Endpoint\n**File:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/notifications.ts`\n\nThis endpoint handles:\n- **GET /api/notifications** - Get all non-archived notifications for the authenticated user\n  - Returns list of notifications with fields: id, type, issue_id, description, read, archived, created_at, issue_identifier, issue_title\n  - Requires Bearer token authentication\n  \n- **PUT /api/notifications/{notificationId}/read** - Mark a single notification as read\n  - Updates the `read` field to true\n  - Returns `{ success: true }`\n  \n- **PUT /api/notifications/{notificationId}/archive** - Archive a notification\n  - Updates the `archived` field to true\n  - Returns `{ success: true }`\n\n### 2. Notifications Count API Endpoint\n**File:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/notifications-count.ts`\n\n- **GET /api/notifications-count** - Get count of unread, non-archived notifications\n  - Returns `{ count: number }`\n  - Requires Bearer token authentication\n\n### 3. Auth/Login API Endpoint\n**File:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/login.ts`\n\n- **POST /api/login** - Authenticate user and get session token\n  - Request body: `{ email: string, password: string }`\n  - Response: `{ user: { id, name, email }, token: string }`\n  - Token is valid for 30 days\n  - Uses PBKDF2 password hashing with SHA-512\n\n### 4. Teams API Endpoint\n**File:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/teams.ts`\n\n- **GET /api/teams** - List all teams with metadata\n  - Returns: `{ teams: Array<{ id, name, identifier, description, member_count, active_cycle_name }> }`\n  - Use this to get dynamic team IDs\n  \n- **GET /api/teams/{teamId}** - Get specific team details with members\n  - Returns: `{ team, members, availableMembers }`\n  \n- **POST /api/teams** - Create new team\n- **PUT /api/teams/{teamId}** - Update team\n- **DELETE /api/teams/{teamId}** - Delete team\n\n### 5. Inbox Page Component\n**File:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/Inbox.tsx`\n\nThe Inbox page:\n- Displays notifications via `<NotificationList>` component\n- Uses Redux state for notifications, loading state, and unreadCount\n- Fetches notifications on mount if token exists\n- Shows unread count badge in the title\n\n### 6. Notification Display & Marking As Read\n\n**NotificationList Component** (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/NotificationList.tsx`):\n- Displays list of notification rows\n- Shows \"You're all caught up!\" when no notifications\n- Displays unread count in header\n\n**NotificationRow Component** (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/NotificationRow.tsx`):\n- Renders individual notification with type icon, issue identifier, description, timestamp\n- On click: marks notification as read (if not already) and navigates to issue detail\n- Archive button: removes notification from list\n- Supports keyboard navigation (Enter key)\n\n**Redux Slice** (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/notificationsSlice.ts`):\n- `fetchNotifications()` - Gets all notifications via `/api/notifications`\n- `markNotificationRead(notificationId)` - Marks as read via `/api/notifications/{id}/read`\n- `archiveNotification(notificationId)` - Archives via `/api/notifications/{id}/archive`\n- `fetchUnreadCount()` - Gets count via `/api/notifications-count`\n- Manages state: items[], unreadCount, loading\n\n### 7. Playwright Configuration\n**File:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n\nKey configuration:\n- Test directory: `./tests`\n- Base URL: `http://localhost:8888`\n- Timeout: 60 seconds (actions 15 seconds)\n- Uses Replay.io for recording\n- Reporter: Replay, JSON, and HTML\n- Uses Chromium with Replay devices\n- Fully parallel execution"}],"totalDurationMs":16013,"totalTokens":35883,"totalToolUseCount":13,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4884,"cache_read_input_tokens":29920,"output_tokens":1072,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4884},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
